{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/574548-maximizing-speed","id":574548,"title":"Maximizing Speed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-30T18:32:32-07:00","id":574548,"title":"Maximizing Speed","content":"I have a recurring background character in a Vampire game I'm storytelling, sort of a Kindred Kourier service (who may or may not be Pheippides, the original Marathon runner), and just for fun, I wanted to try to maximize speed. Thus far, I've been able to get him fast enough to get from LA to NYC (with the Forced March devotion) in a little over 9 hours, at 270 MPH. I was just wondering if it was possible to get faster than that?<br /> <br /> What I have is a Strength 10, Dexterity 10, Vigor 5, Celerity 5 vampire with Fleet-Footed (***) and riding a bicycle. Keep in mind that I'm trying to maximize speed from body power, so motorized vehicles are no good.<br /> <br /> If it helps for your calculations, Speed is effectively in feet per second (1 yard in 1 three-second turn), doubled for skipping your action to run full tilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 07-01-2015, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T02:14:30-07:00","id":574917,"title":"","content":"That must be some strong bicycle, if it survives someone pedaling with Strength 10 and Vigor 5. So unless he has some magical bicycle it's not going to work.<br /> <br /> Maybe he should use a skateboard (or roller/inline skates, but those have no stats). Less moving parts that can break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T02:51:01-07:00","id":574939,"title":"","content":"Celerity (which you didn't list so I'm assuming you didn't count) is an obvious one, though only really for &quot;short&quot; distances. I put &quot;short&quot; in quotes because when you're dealing with speeds like 270mph, even a 3 second turn will get you pretty far. And since you're apparently giving him BP 10, he'll have the blood pool to keep it up for a little while at least. You're looking at about 1620mph or so for 3 seconds per Vitae spent at Celerity 5. That's 1.35 miles per vitae. That's also over twice the speed of sound, so while it's a bit expensive for long-distance deliveries, I guess he could defend against any thieves with gods-damned sonic boom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T05:35:20-07:00","id":575084,"title":"","content":"Well it's not quite the way you were thinking, but if a game includes the children of thorns then the couriers could get to different cities as quickly as they can arrange for another covenant member to get to a mirror.<br /> <br /> Or if using that upcoming dragon coil that allows one to take supernatural merits, you could have vampires who can walk from city to city in a turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 07-01-2015, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T07:01:00-07:00","id":575167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/574548-maximizing-speed?p=574939#post574939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celerity (which you didn't list so I'm assuming you didn't count) is an obvious one, though only really for &quot;short&quot; distances. I put &quot;short&quot; in quotes because when you're dealing with speeds like 270mph, even a 3 second turn will get you pretty far. And since you're apparently giving him BP 10, he'll have the blood pool to keep it up for a little while at least. You're looking at about 1620mph or so for 3 seconds per Vitae spent at Celerity 5. That's 1.35 miles per vitae. That's also over twice the speed of sound, so while it's a bit expensive for long-distance deliveries, I guess he could defend against any thieves with gods-damned sonic boom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I forgot to mention Celerity, although it's included in the calculation. I also have this guy having the Forced March Devotion (Carthians), so keeping it up long periods isn't an issue.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And as for expense, with the really extreme deliveries, he's paid in Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T08:52:03-07:00","id":575279,"title":"","content":"While how big an impact it has depends on edition (you didn't specific and Forced March is 1e even if each to convert over), you can pick up Protean for a bit more of a boost. In VtR 2e, Protean 2 gets you a +4 speed for one of the aspects, In VtR 1e, bat-form's Speed calculations were actually pretty insane with high Vigor IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T00:54:59-07:00","id":578378,"title":"","content":"At first Protean wouldn't help him because of the bicycle, but assuming that he really would need a Enhanced bicycle to handle such mechanical stress, I think it wouldn't be an issue to acquire one that can put the Protean effects to good use. In that case, Protean 2 could grant Patagia, Prehensile Tail and Quadripedal: +4 Speed (before Celerity), more adherence to the vehicle with the tail and the possibility to glide to cut distances here and there. With such velocity, you can glide over an entire town! With Protean 4 you could easily come up with something even better, since it isn't intent to be an exhaustive list. Based on the Patagia-Wings relation, I dare to say you could easily think of something to get between +6 to +10 to your Speed. Keep it low if you want it to be combined with Quadripedal.<br /> <br /> And that bicycle. There ARE rules for all sort of magical itens, so pick your favourite one! An Enhanced Item from Mage can give you a reasonable boost for a few Experiences threw in Merits, and for that type of courrier I do think he would try hard to acquire the best bicycle he can find, and he CAN find the best around. Not looking in the book right now (even because the 2e is coming) I can say that it will be no less than +4 Speed if you put 5 dots on Enhanced Item.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}